<title>POLAND: POLISH OFFICIAL RESERVES UP TO $17.97 BLN IN AUG.</title>
<headline>POLISH OFFICIAL RESERVES UP TO $17.97 BLN IN AUG.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish official foreign currency</p>
<p>reserves grew by $187 million in August to $17.97 billion and</p>
<p>were $6.23 billion higher than a year ago, the National Bank of</p>
<p>Poland said on Monday.</p>
<p>It said official reserves grew $3.00 billion in the</p>
<p>January-August period compared to a $5.71 billion rise in the</p>
<p>corresponding period of last year.</p>
<p>    POLISH RESERVES (bln dlrs)  AUGUST 96   JULY 96   AUGUST 95</p>
<p>    Official reserves		17.97	 17.78     11.74</p>
<p>    Net reserves		     21.93	 21.96     17.40</p>
<p>NOTE - Official reserves are those held by the state. Net</p>
<p>reserves mean the total amount of hard currencies in the whole</p>
<p>banking system.    -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
